{"question": "Junior security engineer Xiao Lin is implementing the "Forgot Password" function for the new Carbon Emission Asset Management Platform. He recalls that during security training, the person in charge, Guohua Yin, emphasized that to prevent user enumeration attacks, all external system messages must remain vague and consistent under all circumstances. Now, he needs to handle a boundary case: when an enterprise account is marked as a 'risky account' and temporarily frozen by the security system due to multiple failed password attempts, and that user tries to reset their password again through the 'Forgot Password' function. In this specific scenario, how should Xiao Lin design the front-end feedback logic?
Options:
{"A": "The baseline specifications for platform secure interaction should be followed. To ensure absolute consistency in anti-enumeration strategies, the system should not set exceptions for any account status. All requests should be processed through the `ERR_POLICY_UNIFIED_RESPONSE_V1` policy, uniformly returning the vague prompt \"If this account is registered, you will receive an email.\" This is the core defense mechanism to prevent attackers from probing account status through response differences.", "B": "Based on the latest security architecture review conclusions, the `ERR_POLICY_LOCKED_ACCOUNT_V1` policy should be applied. This policy aims to achieve a balance between 'risk awareness and user-friendliness': on one hand, it returns a clear account lockout prompt to the frontend; on the other hand, to ensure users' right to know and quick recovery, the system still asynchronously triggers an email sending a notification with unlock instructions. This ensures that alerts are issued without interrupting the user's self-service recovery path.", "C": "Based on the tiered alert design under the Zero Trust architecture, the `WARN_POLICY_SUSPICIOUS_ACTIVITY_V2` policy should be invoked. This policy decouples front-end responses from back-end handling: the front end only returns a generic error code that contains no status information, while high-risk logs are recorded in the background and the Security Operations Center (SOC) is notified for manual investigation, preventing any internal status from being exposed to potential attackers.", "D": "Based on the platform's core error policy dictionary, the system needs to check the account status. If the status is `ACCOUNT_STATUS_LOCKED`, the `ERR_POLICY_LOCKED_ACCOUNT_V1` policy is applied, which aborts the email sending process and returns a clear \"account locked\" message to the frontend. For other statuses, the standard process is followed to return a vague message."}
Begin your answer with the selected option letter and justify it from the records.", "sources": [{"source_id": 1, "record_author": "Guohua Yin", "recorded_at": "2025-05-02 10:15:00", "text": "@Yang Zhao Good question. Regarding the "forgot password" process, our main security consideration is to prevent "user enumeration attacks." Therefore, regardless of whether the email entered by the user exists or not, the feedback message should be consistent, such as "If this email address is registered, you will receive an email containing a password reset link," instead of directly prompting "user does not exist." Please ensure the UI copy adheres to this principle."}, {"source_id": 2, "record_author": "Yang Zhao", "recorded_at": "2025-05-02 09:20:15", "text": "No problem, Boss Chen. I'll check immediately. Also, I'm officially starting today to create high-fidelity UI design mockups for the login, registration, and forgot password pages. I will design based on the existing wireframes and PRD. @Guohua Yin, regarding the "forgot password" process, are there any particular security or usability details I need to pay attention to?"}, {"source_id": 3, "record_author": "Yang Zhao", "recorded_at": "2025-05-08 17:05:00", "text": "Everyone, the high-fidelity UI design for the login/registration/forgot password pages has been officially completed! 🎉 I have uploaded the final version to Figma and meticulously annotated all components and interaction states. @Huilan Chen @Guohua Yin, please conduct the final review. In particular, the forgot password process fully adheres to the security principles previously proposed by Manager Yin, standardizing the prompt copy and avoiding user enumeration risks. https://sd.figma.com/file/20250508/supply-chain-carbon-footprint-login-ui-v1.0"}, {"source_id": 4, "record_author": "Guohua Yin", "recorded_at": "2025-05-08 17:18:00", "text": "Confirmed, the interaction design for "forgot password" meets security requirements. The overall quality of the design draft is very high, great work @Yang Zhao."}, {"source_id": 5, "record_author": "Yang Zhao", "recorded_at": "2025-05-05 10:00:15", "text": "Morning~ I have two tasks today. One is to continue advancing the high-fidelity design of the login/registration page. I will implement the interactive copy for the "forgot password" flow to prevent user enumeration attacks, as mentioned by Guohua Yin last week. The other is to start the high-fidelity design of the new supplier admission process page. I will first study the relevant PRD and flowcharts before starting the design."}, {"source_id": 6, "record_author": "Guohua Yin", "recorded_at": "2025-07-28 11:15:35", "text": "External auditor's account? `LFP_SECURE_GENERIC` this policy returns a unified vague hint, right? Like 'username or password error', instead of 'user does not exist'."}, {"source_id": 7, "record_author": "Qing Wei", "recorded_at": "2025-06-13 14:10:20", "text": "Here's an update on the progress: The complete flow for the "Forgot Password" page has been developed and debugged. The entire process, from entering the email, receiving the verification code, verifying it, to resetting the password, is now fully functional. I've self-tested it several times, including scenarios like incorrect verification codes and mismatched password formats, and all prompts are working correctly. @Minghua Wei, please help arrange regression testing. Thank you!"}, {"source_id": 8, "record_author": "Minghua Wei", "recorded_at": "2025-10-15 09:15:10", "text": "Good morning everyone. Today, I will continue to execute test cases for the user registration and login process. The core test cases were completed yesterday. Today, the focus will be on supplementing and executing various abnormal and boundary scenarios, such as using an already registered email, password format not meeting requirements, and locking an account after consecutive incorrect password attempts."}]}

