uch as incorrect passwords and account lockouts. We found an issue where the back-end returned error messages that were not user-friendly enough, and this has been recorded in Jira."}, {"source_id": 10, "record_author": "Guohua Yin", "recorded_at": "2025-06-09 12:04:12", "text": "Yes, @Xinjie Li. The goal is to unify the feedback output of risk accounts to prevent attackers from probing account status through differences in returns from different interfaces."}, {"source_id": 11, "record_author": "Xinjie Li", "recorded_at": "2025-08-05 15:19:17", "text": "Understood. This strategy is mainly to prevent attacks like username enumeration. For new business modules that require similar login protection in the future, should this strategy be adopted by default? @Mingzhi Li"}]}

