{"question": "Xiao A, I have an urgent matter here. The real-time heart rate dashboard for health monitoring is scheduled for a client demo next week, but currently, it uses polling, and the data updates too slowly, leading to a poor user experience. I've decided not to wait for a unified upgrade and will directly refactor it to WebSocket. I'm familiar with this and can get it done today. This will significantly improve the demo's effectiveness. I'll go ahead and start working on it, okay?
Options:
{"A": "Feasible, but compatibility needs to be considered. Given that backend services are not yet fully standardized, it is recommended that the frontend use the `sockjs-client` library. This library can automatically degrade to polling when WebSocket is unavailable, ensuring a smooth transition and the stability of online features.", "B": "WebSocket is not recommended. At a recent technical review meeting, architect Yu Wang pointed out that the WebSocket solution is too cumbersome for unidirectional data push scenarios. The meeting decided to recommend using the lighter Server-Sent Events (SSE) technology instead. You can research this solution.", "C": "Yes, this plan has been updated. Mingzhi Li announced at last week's (around October 8) backend architecture meeting that the core module of the message push service has passed acceptance testing and its performance is stable. He has approved that new features can directly use WebSocket for development, and no longer need to wait for a unified upgrade. Please proceed with confidence and update the technical documentation upon completion.", "D": "Not yet. According to Mingzhi Li, the project lead's previous plan, because the backend message push service is not yet fully ready, all tasks requiring dynamic refreshing should currently be implemented using polling. Please continue to use polling, and the team will organize a unified upgrade once the service is stable."}
Begin your answer with the selected option letter and justify it from the records.", "sources": [{"source_id": 1, "record_author": "Huihong Fu", "recorded_at": "2025-10-02 14:45:05", "text": "Alright! I'll get to it! First, I'll configure Kafka's topics. I feel like I can get the message producer and consumer demos done today. Hehe, a little excited! 😆"}, {"source_id": 2, "record_author": "Weijun Xue", "recorded_at": "2025-10-17 16:35:10", "text": "@Huihong Tian @Li Jin Awesome! Looking forward to seeing the demo next week. This feature is crucial for improving user activity."}, {"source_id": 3, "record_author": "Peng Sun", "recorded_at": "2025-11-17 10:05:00", "text": "@Zihao Wan Okay, you go ahead and verify. I'm also looking at a few other complex queries that link user tags and health plans, and I feel there's room for optimization there too. The slow query optimization for this project has drawn on the experience from the previous diagnosis and treatment system, and the efficiency has improved significantly."}, {"source_id": 4, "record_author": "Guoxin Pan", "recorded_at": "2025-04-08 15:05:10", "text": "@Hao Lv Here I am. The PRD has detailed definitions, but I'll emphasize them here again: The highest priority for the Dashboard is the user's real-time heart rate and daily step count, followed by a sleep quality overview. For the historical data page, in addition to the regular daily/weekly/monthly view switching, it also needs to support the overlay comparison function for different metrics, such as a trend comparison of heart rate and blood oxygen."}, {"source_id": 5, "record_author": "Dong He", "recorded_at": "2025-01-28 10:32:14", "text": "Yes, 2019 users can upgrade directly. But 2016 users will have to first upgrade to 2019, and then to SE. This is quite a bit of work, we need to start scheduling it."}, {"source_id": 6, "record_author": "Huihong Fu", "recorded_at": "2025-03-17 10:35:45", "text": "Received, Boss Li. I've used Tencent Cloud in previous projects, so I have some experience. I'll get two of my team members to split up and research the documentation and demos of these providers. We'll provide a preliminary comparative analysis report before this Wednesday."}, {"source_id": 7, "record_author": "Guoxin Pan", "recorded_at": "2025-10-13 14:47:21", "text": "Great! This is exactly the performance guarantee our real-time CGM monitoring function needs. Once the data link is isolated, the real-time refresh experience on the front end will definitely improve significantly! 🚀"}, {"source_id": 8, "record_author": "Junxin Yuan", "recorded_at": "2025-09-23 09:25:40", "text": "Good morning, Boss Li. Regarding the real-time health data aggregation interface, the interface design and preliminary planning for the database query solution were completed yesterday. Today, we're officially entering the coding phase. I'll start by implementing a basic version that can aggregate real-time heart rate and blood pressure data in minute-level windows. I'm currently writing the SQL for data queries."}]}

